      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Jack Setters Arena, built in 1974, is Calgary’s first indoor ice rink named after a dedicated minor‑hockey volunteer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.millicanogden.com/community-history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Millican‑Ogden is one of Calgary’s oldest communities, with roots tracing back to the early 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.millicanogden.com/community-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ogden was officially established in 1912, long before the surrounding industrial areas developed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ogden%2C_Calgary",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The former Royal Canadian Legion building in Ogden served as a community centre before its demolition in 2026.",
